    "https://careers.usc.edu.au/jobs/payroll-officer-unisc-moreton-bay-queensland-australia": {
      "title": "Payroll Officer",
      "description": "Payroll Officer - UniSC Moreton Bay, Queensland, Australia Contact Us Candidate login Explore Opportunities Academic jobs Professional jobs Casual jobs Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander jobs Recruitment process Employer information Applicant Settings Kiosk mode < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNITIES Payroll Officer 1 Moreton Parade, UniSC Moreton Bay, Queensland, Australia, 4502 Administration / Admin Support L5 $82,843 - $93,358 +17% super People and Culture Professional Show More Show Less Full-Time Add to favourites View favourites People and Culture | UniSC Moreton Bay, Petrie Level 5, $82,843 - $93,358 p.a., plus up to 17% employer superannuation Full-time, Ongoing appointment The Opportunity At UniSC, our People and Culture team is dedicated to creating an exceptional employee experience that enables our people to thrive. As a Payroll Officer, you will play a key role in ensuring every staff member is paid accurately, on time, and in accordance with legislative and University requirements. Supporting the delivery of the University's fortnightly payroll, you will provide trusted advice on payroll, superannuation, taxation, and employment conditions while maintaining compliance with complex industrial instruments and legislative obligations. Your expertise and attention to detail will contribute to the integrity of our payroll operations and the continuous improvement of systems and processes that enhance service delivery. Working within a collaborative and customer-focused team, you will build positive relationships with colleagues across the University, delivering responsive, high-quality payroll support and helping to ensure a seamless experience for our people. You will Provision of advice on a broad range of payroll and superannuation matters; Contribute to the efficient and effective delivery of the University’s fortnightly payroll functions; and Ensure compliance with relevant legislation, policy and procedures. About you You are a detail-oriented payroll professional who thrives on accuracy, compliance, and delivering exceptional service. With a strong understanding of payroll legislation, industrial instruments, and employment conditions, you enjoy working in a fast-paced environment where precision and deadlines matter. You confidently provide trusted advice, build positive relationships across a diverse organisation, and apply your analytical and problem-solving skills to resolve complex payroll matters, identify opportunities for process improvement, and contribute to the continuous enhancement of payroll services. You will possess: Extensive experience in the accurate preparation and completion of fortnightly payroll processes within a large organisation, including demonstrated knowledge of superannuation and taxation legislation; Strong analytical skills with expertise in structured and ad hoc reporting, and proficiency in the use of a complex HRIS, preferably PeopleSoft; Experience providing accurate advice and dealing with enquiries involving interpreting employment conditions, policies, procedures and guidelines while providing quality customer service; The capacity to exercise sound judgement, take initiative and solve problems, as required; Excellent computing and word processing skills with high-level experience in the development and maintenance of databases and spreadsheets; and High level organisational and interpersonal skills including the ability to communicate effectively both verbally and in writing. Don't meet every requirement? At UniSC, we understand that your work and life experiences can be just as valuable. If you're excited about this role but your CV doesn't align perfectly with our position description, we encourage you to apply anyway. You may be just the right candidate for this or one of our many other opportunities. UniSC is an equal opportunity employer, committed to diversity and inclusion. We encourage applications from all backgrounds, including those with disabilities, women in STEM, First Nations Peoples, and individuals of diverse cultures, genders, abilities, and experiences. We value achievement relative to opportunity and encourage your commentary on your achievements in this context. For additional support during the application process, please contact us at unisc-careers@usc.edu.au or call +61 7 5430 2830. How to apply All applications must be lodged through our website. To apply please visit our website at: Careers at UniSC We will be reviewing applications and contacting suitable candidates throughout the duration of this advertisement. We strongly encourage you to submit your interest as soon as possible. Position description: 494704_Payroll Officer.pdf Your completed application must include: a resume and a statement of suitability (not to exceed two pages) , which will be reviewed in alignment to the specified selection criteria as outlined within the position description. Further information regarding how to prepare your application is available on our website: Join our team. Have questions or want to know more? For a confidential discussion, please contact: Emma Bayles Associate Director, Employee Experience – People and Culture Telephone: 07 5459 4492 Email: ebayles@usc.edu.au We would love the opportunity to get to know you better, but we know it works both ways. To get to know a little more about us, visit us at: Welcome to UniSC and LinkedIn Life UniSC values a diverse and talented workforce and invites applications from candidates who already have legal work rights in Australia. UniSC does not accept unsolicited applications. For agency inquiries, contact unisc-careers@usc.edu.au Discover UniSC We’re all about doing work that matters, connecting with great people, and being part of an incredible journey. While we’re not the largest university, we are one of the fastest growing in Australia, now with over 2,000 staff across five campuses in South East Queensland and an expanding presence in major capital cities, and we’re making a big impact every day through ground-breaking research, a strong commitment to sustainability, high-performance sport, and award-winning alumni. We are committed to delivering high-quality research and teaching that address major global and regional challenges, with established and emerging strengths in sustainability, environmental systems, biodiversity, aquaculture, preventative health and regional resilience. Our research excellence is internationally recognised through strong performance in global benchmarking, including leading rankings in the 2025 Times Higher Education (THE) Impact Rankings for “Zero Hunger,” “Climate Action” and “Life on Land.” UniSC is also recognised for its teaching excellence, with a strong emphasis on student success, innovative and engaging learning experiences, and strong graduate outcomes that equip learners to make meaningful contributions in their chosen fields. As the only university operating within three UNESCO Biosphere Reserves and a UNESCO World Heritage Site, UniSC is uniquely positioned to leverage its natural environment to advance impactful research, teaching and partnerships that support sustainable futures, with sustainability embedded across all aspects of our teaching, research and operations. We foster a collaborative and supportive environment that encourages continuous professional development and provides the tools and resources to grow your career. We value the contributions of every team member and the role they play in our culture and success. We’re not afraid to do things differently, and we’re looking for people who share our values and want to be part of a team working together to make a meaningful difference to local and global challenges. Our Culture & Benefits: Our collaborative, passionate and welcoming culture is what really sets us apart. Modern teaching & research facilities. Professional development and career pathway opportunities. We are a proud recipient of the prestigious Athena SWAN Bronze Award, granted as part of the Science in Australia Gender Equity (SAGE) initiative. Flexible work arrangements & generous leave options. Salary packing options + 17% Super. EAP, fitness passport & discounted private health. < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNTIES About UniSC For more information about UniSC's employment benefits and culture, including employee blogs, visit our employer information page . Recommended for you Clinical Practice Educator, Nutrition and Dietetics UniSC Sunshine Coast. UniSC Moreton Bay Academic, LB $118,481 - $140,567 +17% super, School of Health Shape the future of nutrition and dietetics through high-quality clinical education, student supervision and meaningful industry partnerships. Technician (Nursing and Midwifery) UniSC Caboolture. UniSC Fraser Coast. UniSC Gympie. UniSC Moreton Bay Academic Support Unit, L5 $82,843 - $93,358 +17% super, Technical Support Join a growing UniSC team, with multiple newly created opportunities supporting the expansion of our Nursing and Midwifery programs. Bring your clinical or technical expertise and make a difference to the next generation of health professionals. Work Integrated Learning (WIL) Placement Officer UniSC Sunshine Coast Academic Support Unit, Administration / Admin Support, Individual contributor, L5 $82,843 - $93,358 +17% super, Professional Help students turn learning into real-world impact through meaningful industry experiences that shape future careers. Work Integrated Learning (WIL) Placement Officer UniSC Moreton Bay Academic Support Unit, Administration / Admin Support, Individual contributor, L5 $82,843 - $93,358 +17% super, Professional Help shape meaningful industry experiences that transform student futures. LEGAL Privacy Copyright Disclaimer Right to Information Data Collection Preferences The University of the Sunshine Coast acknowledges the Traditional Custodians of the land on which we live, work and study. We pay our respects to local Indigenous Elders past, present and emerging and recognise the strength, resilience and capacity of all Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people. ABN 28 441 859 157 | CRICOS Provider No. 01595D | TEQSA Provider No. PRV12082 Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. By continuing, you agree that you have read our Privacy Statement I do not accept I accept"
    },
    "https://careers.usc.edu.au/jobs/professor-of-education-unisc-sunshine-coast-qld-australia-unisc-moreton-bay-queensland": {
      "title": "Professor of Education",
      "description": "Professor of Education - UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia - UniSC Moreton Bay, Queensland, Australia Contact Us Candidate login Explore Opportunities Academic jobs Professional jobs Casual jobs Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander jobs Recruitment process Employer information Applicant Settings Kiosk mode < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNITIES Professor of Education 90 Sippy Downs Drive, UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia, 4556 1 Moreton Parade, UniSC Moreton Bay, Queensland, Australia, 4502 Academic LE $224,480 +17% super School of Education and Tertiary Access Full-Time Add to favourites View favourites School of Education and Tertiary Access | UniSC Sunshine Coast, Sippy Downs or UniSC Moreton Bay, Petrie Academic Level E, $224,480 p.a., plus up to 17% employer superannuation Full-time, fixed term appointment until July 2031 The Opportunity This is a rare opportunity to join a university where your influence will be visible, valued and far-reaching. As Professor of Education, you will play a defining role in shaping the future direction of education at UniSC, contributing to a high-performing and collaborative academic community that is ambitious in its goals and deeply connected to the communities it serves. Unlike larger institutions, where leadership can be dispersed across extensive structures, UniSC offers the opportunity to work within a close-knit School where relationships matter, decisions are made with agility, and outstanding academics have the ability to directly influence strategy, culture, research performance and educational innovation. Working closely with the Dean and senior colleagues, you will provide research leadership, strengthen academic capability, mentor the next generation of researchers and educators, and build partnerships that deliver meaningful impact across education, industry and the wider community. Through your leadership, you will help position UniSC at the forefront of contemporary educational research and practice while supporting future-ready graduates who make a difference in the world. Why UniSC? At UniSC, you'll join a university that combines the ambition and impact of a rapidly growing institution with the collegiality and accessibility of a smaller academic community. Our size is one of our strengths. It enables genuine collaboration across disciplines, close connections between leaders and academics, and opportunities to see the direct impact of your work on students, colleagues and the broader community. As part of the School of Education and Tertiary Access, you'll work alongside a passionate, high-performing team that values scholarship, innovation, inclusion and mutual support. It's an environment where talented academics can do their best work while contributing to something bigger than themselves. In this role you will: Provide strategic academic leadership that strengthens the School's research capability, learning and teaching excellence, academic culture and future direction. Lead an internationally recognised research program, developing ambitious research agendas, securing competitive external funding, producing high-quality outputs and translating research into meaningful social, cultural, economic and educational impact. Build research capability and academic talent, mentoring Early and Mid-Career Researchers, supporting Higher Degree by Research candidates and developing collaborative, interdisciplinary research teams. Champion excellence and innovation in learning and teaching, providing scholarly leadership in curriculum and program development, contemporary pedagogy, assessment and student success. Build influential partnerships across regional, national and international networks, creating opportunities for research collaboration, educational innovation, professional engagement and broader community impact. Contribute to School and University leadership, governance and strategic decision-making, helping build a high-performing, collegial and inclusive academic culture. This is a rare opportunity to join a university with an ambitious vision for education and research and to make a lasting contribution to students, the profession and the communities UniSC serves. For more information on the School of Education and Tertiary Access, please visit us online: School of Education and Tertiary Access Relocation support We welcome applications from outstanding candidates across Australia and internationally and offer relocation assistance to support a smooth transition. Choosing UniSC means choosing more than a career opportunity. It means joining a region renowned for its exceptional quality of life. Whether based at our Sunshine Coast campus in Sippy Downs or our Moreton Bay campus in Petrie, you'll enjoy access to world-class beaches, national parks, vibrant local communities, excellent schools, and an enviable outdoor lifestyle, all within easy reach of Brisbane and international travel connections. Many of our staff are drawn to UniSC by the unique combination of professional opportunity and lifestyle balance, and stay because they become part of a welcoming, connected and collaborative community. About you You are a respected and influential academic leader who combines scholarly excellence with a genuine commitment to people, partnerships and purpose. Recognised for your research achievements and thought leadership, you have a track record of building capability in others, fostering collaborative research cultures and creating meaningful impact through education. You are energised by the opportunity to contribute within a university where your leadership will be highly visible and where you can help shape strategic direction, develop future academic talent and strengthen the University's reputation nationally and internationally. To excel in this role, you will bring: A doctoral qualification in a relevant field, together with extensive experience as an academic leader and a record of significant contribution to the development of your discipline. International academic standing, with an established reputation and recognised contribution to education and your discipline at national and international levels. A distinguished research profile, demonstrated through sustained high-quality research, significant research outputs, competitive external funding, research impact and a strong record of Higher Degree by Research supervision. Research leadership and capability building, with the ability to lead research programs and teams, mentor Early and Mid-Career Researchers, strengthen research culture and develop research capability across the School. Excellence and leadership in learning and teaching, including a strong record of innovative curriculum and program development, contemporary teaching practice and demonstrable influence on educational practice and student success. Strategic academic leadership, with the ability to contribute to School and University strategy, governance and decision-making, while fostering a high-performing, inclusive and collegial academic culture. A strong record of engagement and partnership, with the ability to establish and sustain productive regional, national and international relationships that enhance research, learning and teaching, and deliver meaningful outcomes for the University and wider community. Vision for the future of education, with the capacity to translate research, teaching and professional expertise into meaningful impact, strengthen strategic partnerships and help shape future-ready graduates. Don't meet every requirement? At UniSC, we understand that your work and life experiences can be just as valuable. If you're excited about this role but your CV doesn't align perfectly with our position description, we encourage you to apply anyway. You may be just the right candidate for this or one of our many other opportunities. UniSC is an equal opportunity employer, committed to diversity and inclusion. We encourage applications from all backgrounds, including those with disabilities, women in STEM, First Nations Peoples, and individuals of diverse cultures, genders, abilities, and experiences. We value achievement relative to opportunity and encourage your commentary on your achievements in this context. For additional support during the application process, please contact us at unisc-careers@usc.edu.au or call +61 7 5430 2830 . How to apply All applications must be lodged through our website. To apply please visit our website at: Careers at UniSC Position description: 494762_Professor in Education.pdf Applications for this position close midnight, Monday 14 September 2026. Your completed application must include: Resume; A cover letter of no more than one page, outlining the skills, knowledge, experience and qualities you would bring to the role and UniSC; and A response to the key selection criteria, demonstrating how your experience and achievements align with the requirements of the position (to be responded to within the online application form). Further information regarding how to prepare your application is available on our website: Join our team Have questions or want to know more? For a confidential discussion, please contact: Professor Kate Williams Dean, School of Education and Tertiary Access Phone: 07 5456 3039 Email: DeanSETA@usc.edu.au We would love the opportunity to get to know you better, but we know it works both ways. To get to know a little more about us, visit us at: Welcome to UniSC and LinkedIn Life UniSC values a diverse and talented workforce and invites applications from candidates who already have legal work rights in Australia. UniSC does not accept unsolicited applications. For agency inquiries, contact unisc-careers@usc.edu.au Discover UniSC At UniSC, we're proving that size doesn't define impact. As one of Australia's fastest-growing universities, we've built a reputation for combining academic excellence, meaningful research and strong community connection. Our success is driven by talented people who value collaboration over hierarchy, ambition over bureaucracy, and the opportunity to make a genuine difference. What sets UniSC apart is the way we work. Here, you'll be part of a connected academic community where relationships matter, ideas are welcomed, and exceptional people have the opportunity to influence outcomes, lead change and see the impact of their contribution. We are committed to delivering high-quality research and teaching that address major global and regional challenges, with established and emerging strengths in sustainability, environmental systems, biodiversity, aquaculture, preventative health and regional resilience. Our research excellence is internationally recognised through strong performance in global benchmarking, including leading rankings in the 2025 Times Higher Education (THE) Impact Rankings for “Zero Hunger,” “Climate Action” and “Life on Land.” UniSC is also recognised for its teaching excellence, with a strong emphasis on student success, innovative and engaging learning experiences, and strong graduate outcomes that equip learners to make meaningful contributions in their chosen fields. As the only university operating within three UNESCO Biosphere Reserves and a UNESCO World Heritage Site, UniSC is uniquely positioned to leverage its natural environment to advance impactful research, teaching and partnerships that support sustainable futures, with sustainability embedded across all aspects of our teaching, research and operations. We foster a collaborative and supportive environment that encourages continuous professional development and provides the tools and resources to grow your career. We value the contributions of every team member and the role they play in our culture and success. We’re not afraid to do things differently, and we’re looking for people who share our values and want to be part of a team working together to make a meaningful difference to local and global challenges. Our Culture & Benefits: Our collaborative, passionate and welcoming culture is what really sets us apart. Modern teaching & research facilities. Professional development and career pathway opportunities. We are a proud recipient of the prestigious Athena SWAN Bronze Award, granted as part of the Science in Australia Gender Equity (SAGE) initiative. Flexible work arrangements & generous leave options. Salary packaging options + 17% Super. EAP, fitness passport & discounted private health. < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNTIES About UniSC For more information about UniSC's employment benefits and culture, including employee blogs, visit our employer information page . Recommended for you Clinical Practice Educator, Nutrition and Dietetics UniSC Sunshine Coast. UniSC Moreton Bay Academic, LB $118,481 - $140,567 +17% super, School of Health Shape the future of nutrition and dietetics through high-quality clinical education, student supervision and meaningful industry partnerships. Technician (Nursing and Midwifery) UniSC Caboolture. UniSC Fraser Coast. UniSC Gympie. UniSC Moreton Bay Academic Support Unit, L5 $82,843 - $93,358 +17% super, Technical Support Join a growing UniSC team, with multiple newly created opportunities supporting the expansion of our Nursing and Midwifery programs. Bring your clinical or technical expertise and make a difference to the next generation of health professionals. Work Integrated Learning (WIL) Placement Officer UniSC Sunshine Coast Academic Support Unit, Administration / Admin Support, Individual contributor, L5 $82,843 - $93,358 +17% super, Professional Help students turn learning into real-world impact through meaningful industry experiences that shape future careers. Work Integrated Learning (WIL) Placement Officer UniSC Moreton Bay Academic Support Unit, Administration / Admin Support, Individual contributor, L5 $82,843 - $93,358 +17% super, Professional Help shape meaningful industry experiences that transform student futures. LEGAL Privacy Copyright Disclaimer Right to Information Data Collection Preferences The University of the Sunshine Coast acknowledges the Traditional Custodians of the land on which we live, work and study. We pay our respects to local Indigenous Elders past, present and emerging and recognise the strength, resilience and capacity of all Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people. ABN 28 441 859 157 | CRICOS Provider No. 01595D | TEQSA Provider No. PRV12082 Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. By continuing, you agree that you have read our Privacy Statement I do not accept I accept"
    },
    "https://careers.usc.edu.au/jobs/clinical-trial-associate-unisc-southbank-qld-australia": {
      "title": "Clinical Trial Associate",
      "description": "Clinical Trial Associate - UniSC SouthBank, QLD, Australia Contact Us Candidate login Explore Opportunities Academic jobs Professional jobs Casual jobs Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander jobs Recruitment process Employer information Applicant Settings Kiosk mode < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNITIES Clinical Trial Associate 32 Cordelia Street, UniSC SouthBank, QLD, Australia, 4101 Clinical Trials Individual contributor L5 $82,843 - $93,358 +17% super Professional Show More Show Less Full-Time Add to favourites View favourites UniSC Clinical Trials | UniSC SouthBank, South Brisbane Level 5, $82,843 - $93,358 p.a., plus up to 17% employer superannuation Full-time (36.25 hours per week), 2 year fixed-term appointment The Opportunity Join our team and play a vital role in advancing clinical research! As a key member of UniSC Clinical Trials, you’ll ensure all trial activities comply with ICH Good Clinical Practice, ethical protocols, UniSC Clinical Trials Standard Operating Procedures, and regulatory requirements. Your expertise will help drive high-quality, compliant research that makes a real impact. If you're passionate about clinical research excellence, we’d love to hear from you! Please note , this role requires flexibility to travel to different clinical trial sites as needed, and to work outside standard business hours to support confinement studies and other time-sensitive trial activities. You may also be required to participate in a 24/7 on-call or confinement roster. For more information, please visit us online: UniSC Clinical Trials You will Support the Clinical Trials Co-ordinator (CTC) and other clinical trials staff with all Human Research Ethics Committee (HREC) approved protocol requirements across the clinical trial life cycle in accordance with appropriate training and experience; and Work collaboratively with the UniSC Clinical Trials (UniSC CT) team, sponsors and monitors to ensure high quality and safe conduct of clinical trials conducted by UniSC CT. About you You’re a proactive problem-solver who exercises sound judgment and takes initiative when needed. With strong computer literacy, including advanced skills in the Microsoft Suite and experience with databases, you work efficiently and effectively. You thrive in dynamic environments, adapting quickly to new challenges while maintaining accuracy, attention to detail, and high-quality outcomes. You will possess: Degree qualification in Health Science/Bio-Medical Science or similar; or a certificate level qualification; or an equivalent combination of relevant experience, education, and training; Knowledge of ICH Good Clinical Practice highly regarded; Exercise sound judgement, take initiative and solve problems, as required; Strong computer literacy including proficiency with the Microsoft suite of tools and experience with software programs including databases; and Prior experience within a clinical research environment is preferred. Don't meet every requirement? At UniSC, we understand that your work and life experiences can be just as valuable. If you're excited about this role but your CV doesn't align perfectly with our position description, we encourage you to apply anyway. You may be just the right candidate for this or one of our many other opportunities. UniSC is an equal opportunity employer, committed to diversity and inclusion. We encourage applications from all backgrounds, including those with disabilities, women in STEM, First Nations Peoples, and individuals of diverse cultures, genders, abilities, and experiences. We value achievement relative to opportunity and encourage your commentary on your achievements in this context. For additional support during the application process, please contact us at unisc-careers@usc.edu.au or call +61 7 5430 2830. How to apply All applications must be lodged through our website. To apply please visit our website at: Careers at UniSC Applications for this position close midnight, Wednesday 16 September 2026. Position description: 494818_Clinical Trials Associate.pdf Your completed application must include: a resume and a statement of suitability (not to exceed two pages), which will be reviewed in alignment to the specified selection criteria as outlined within the position description. Further information regarding how to prepare your application is available on our website: Join our team. Have questions or want to know more? For a confidential discussion, please contact: Freya Letchford-Cross Team Leader, Clinical Trials - UniSC Clinical Trials Telephone: 07 5456 5122 Email: fletchfordcros@usc.edu.au We would love the opportunity to get to know you better, but we know it works both ways. To get to know a little more about us, visit us at: Welcome to UniSC and LinkedIn Life UniSC values a diverse and talented workforce and invites applications from candidates who already have legal work rights in Australia. UniSC does not accept unsolicited applications. For agency inquiries, contact unisc-careers@usc.edu.au Discover UniSC We’re all about doing work that matters, connecting with great people, and being part of an incredible journey. While we’re not the largest university, we are one of the fastest growing in Australia, now with over 2,000 staff across five campuses in South East Queensland and an expanding presence in major capital cities, and we’re making a big impact every day through ground-breaking research, a strong commitment to sustainability, high-performance sport, and award-winning alumni. We are committed to delivering high-quality research and teaching that address major global and regional challenges, with established and emerging strengths in sustainability, environmental systems, biodiversity, aquaculture, preventative health and regional resilience. Our research excellence is internationally recognised through strong performance in global benchmarking, including leading rankings in the 2025 Times Higher Education (THE) Impact Rankings for “Zero Hunger,” “Climate Action” and “Life on Land.” UniSC is also recognised for its teaching excellence, with a strong emphasis on student success, innovative and engaging learning experiences, and strong graduate outcomes that equip learners to make meaningful contributions in their chosen fields. As the only university operating within three UNESCO Biosphere Reserves and a UNESCO World Heritage Site, UniSC is uniquely positioned to leverage its natural environment to advance impactful research, teaching and partnerships that support sustainable futures, with sustainability embedded across all aspects of our teaching, research and operations. We foster a collaborative and supportive environment that encourages continuous professional development and provides the tools and resources to grow your career. We value the contributions of every team member and the role they play in our culture and success. We’re not afraid to do things differently, and we’re looking for people who share our values and want to be part of a team working together to make a meaningful difference to local and global challenges. Our Culture & Benefits: Our collaborative, passionate and welcoming culture is what really sets us apart. Modern teaching & research facilities. Professional development and career pathway opportunities. We are a proud recipient of the prestigious Athena SWAN Bronze Award, granted as part of the Science in Australia Gender Equity (SAGE) initiative. Flexible work arrangements & generous leave options. Salary packing options + 17% Super. EAP, fitness passport & discounted private health. < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNTIES About UniSC For more information about UniSC's employment benefits and culture, including employee blogs, visit our employer information page . Recommended for you Clinical Practice Educator, Nutrition and Dietetics UniSC Sunshine Coast. UniSC Moreton Bay Academic, LB $118,481 - $140,567 +17% super, School of Health Shape the future of nutrition and dietetics through high-quality clinical education, student supervision and meaningful industry partnerships. Technician (Nursing and Midwifery) UniSC Caboolture. UniSC Fraser Coast. UniSC Gympie. UniSC Moreton Bay Academic Support Unit, L5 $82,843 - $93,358 +17% super, Technical Support Join a growing UniSC team, with multiple newly created opportunities supporting the expansion of our Nursing and Midwifery programs. Bring your clinical or technical expertise and make a difference to the next generation of health professionals. Work Integrated Learning (WIL) Placement Officer UniSC Sunshine Coast Academic Support Unit, Administration / Admin Support, Individual contributor, L5 $82,843 - $93,358 +17% super, Professional Help students turn learning into real-world impact through meaningful industry experiences that shape future careers. Work Integrated Learning (WIL) Placement Officer UniSC Moreton Bay Academic Support Unit, Administration / Admin Support, Individual contributor, L5 $82,843 - $93,358 +17% super, Professional Help shape meaningful industry experiences that transform student futures. LEGAL Privacy Copyright Disclaimer Right to Information Data Collection Preferences The University of the Sunshine Coast acknowledges the Traditional Custodians of the land on which we live, work and study. We pay our respects to local Indigenous Elders past, present and emerging and recognise the strength, resilience and capacity of all Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people. ABN 28 441 859 157 | CRICOS Provider No. 01595D | TEQSA Provider No. PRV12082 Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. By continuing, you