    "https://careers.usc.edu.au/jobs/expression-of-interest-gps-other-qualified-medical-practitioners-unisc-sunshine-coast-qld-australia": {
      "title": "Expression of Interest: GPs & other Qualified Medical Practitioners",
      "description": "Expression of Interest: GPs & other Qualified Medical Practitioners - UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia Contact Us Candidate login Explore Opportunities Academic jobs Professional jobs Casual jobs Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander jobs Recruitment process Employer information Applicant Settings Kiosk mode < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNITIES Expression of Interest: GPs & other Qualified Medical Practitioners 90 Sippy Downs Drive, UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia, 4556 Casual Professional Clinical Trials Professional Casual Add to favourites View favourites UniSC Clinical Trials Medical Practitioners UniSC Clinical Trials is inviting expressions of interest  from qualified medical practitioners to join Queensland’s fastest growing network of clinical research professionals across our Sunshine Coast and Morayfield locations. This expression of interest will support current and future opportunities across our expanding portfolio of clinical trials, delivered through a university-backed, globally connected research environment. If you are interested in contributing to innovative healthcare while maintaining flexibility in your clinical career, we welcome your application. About UniSC Clinical Trials UniSC Clinical Trials is one of South-East Queensland’s leading clinical research networks, delivering Phase I–IV trials across a diverse range of therapeutic areas. Supported by dedicated project, regulatory and nursing teams, our investigators work within a high-quality, GCP-compliant environment with strong governance, established primarily international sponsor relationships, and an active pipeline of studies. Our sites span South-East Queensland across Brisbane, Moreton Bay and Sunshine Coast regions with opportunities for flexible scheduling and multiple work locations with continued growth across priority therapeutic areas. About the expression of interest Applications received through this EOI will be  considered for a range of clinician opportunities including: Principal Investigator (PI) roles Sub-Investigator roles Expert Advisor and Patient Referrals While appointments are typically sessional and designed to complement existing clinical practice, the volume of research activity may support full-time involvement for interested clinicians. What we’re looking for We are seeking clinicians who: Are registered medical practitioners in Australia Have an interest in clinical research and advancing evidence-based medicine Demonstrate strong patient care, professionalism, and ethical standards Are interested in flexible, portfolio-based career opportunities Clinicians will be engaged as independent contractors, and must meet the associated contractor requirements, including holding (or being willing to obtain) an Australian Business Number (ABN) and meeting any applicable insurance, compliance, and associated requirements. Previous clinical trial experience not essential. Training, support and mentoring will be provided. Why join UniSC Clinical Trials Flexible, sessional engagement models Opportunity to contribute to globally sponsored research Strong operational and regulatory support Access to multidisciplinary research teams Professional development in clinical research How to apply Your expression of interest must be submitted online, and include: A short statement outlining your interest in clinical research, including any research experience or areas of interest A brief summary of your clinical background, specialty, and/or r esume Preferred work location(s) Applications will be retained in our talent pool and reviewed as opportunities become available. Contact For further information about this opportunity, please contact: Lucas Litewka, Director, UniSC Clinical Trials Centre Phone: +617 5456 5265 Email: llitewka@usc.edu.au OR Jessica Baird, Deputy Director, UniSC Clinical Trials Phone: +61754563556 Email: jbaird@usc.edu.au Join us Be part of a collaborative research environment contributing to the future of healthcare, locally and globally. Discover UniSC We’re all about doing work that matters, connecting with great people, and being part of an incredible journey. While we’re not the largest university, we are one of the fastest growing in Australia, now with over 2,000 staff across five campuses in South East Queensland and an expanding presence in major capital cities, and we’re making a big impact every day through ground-breaking research, a strong commitment to sustainability, high-performance sport, and award-winning alumni. We are committed to delivering high-quality research and teaching that address major global and regional challenges, with established and emerging strengths in sustainability, environmental systems, biodiversity, aquaculture, preventative health and regional resilience. Our research excellence is internationally recognised through strong performance in global benchmarking, including leading rankings in the 2025 Times Higher Education (THE) Impact Rankings for “Zero Hunger,” “Climate Action” and “Life on Land.” UniSC is also recognised for its teaching excellence, with a strong emphasis on student success, innovative and engaging learning experiences, and strong graduate outcomes that equip learners to make meaningful contributions in their chosen fields. As the only university operating within three UNESCO Biosphere Reserves and a UNESCO World Heritage Site, UniSC is uniquely positioned to leverage its natural environment to advance impactful research, teaching and partnerships that support sustainable futures, with sustainability embedded across all aspects of our teaching, research and operations. We foster a collaborative and supportive environment that encourages continuous professional development and provides the tools and resources to grow your career. We value the contributions of every team member and the role they play in our culture and success. We’re not afraid to do things differently, and we’re looking for people who share our values and want to be part of a team working together to make a meaningful difference to local and global challenges. < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNTIES About UniSC For more information about UniSC's employment benefits and culture, including employee blogs, visit our employer information page . Recommended for you Clinical Practice Educator, Nutrition and Dietetics UniSC Sunshine Coast. UniSC Moreton Bay Academic, LB $118,481 - $140,567 +17% super, School of Health Shape the future of nutrition and dietetics through high-quality clinical education, student supervision and meaningful industry partnerships. Technician (Nursing and Midwifery) UniSC Caboolture. UniSC Fraser Coast. UniSC Gympie. UniSC Moreton Bay Academic Support Unit, L5 $82,843 - $93,358 +17% super, Technical Support Join a growing UniSC team, with multiple newly created opportunities supporting the expansion of our Nursing and Midwifery programs. Bring your clinical or technical expertise and make a difference to the next generation of health professionals. Work Integrated Learning (WIL) Placement Officer UniSC Sunshine Coast Academic Support Unit, Administration / Admin Support, Individual contributor, L5 $82,843 - $93,358 +17% super, Professional Help students turn learning into real-world impact through meaningful industry experiences that shape future careers. Work Integrated Learning (WIL) Placement Officer UniSC Moreton Bay Academic Support Unit, Administration / Admin Support, Individual contributor, L5 $82,843 - $93,358 +17% super, Professional Help shape meaningful industry experiences that transform student futures. LEGAL Privacy Copyright Disclaimer Right to Information Data Collection Preferences The University of the Sunshine Coast acknowledges the Traditional Custodians of the land on which we live, work and study. We pay our respects to local Indigenous Elders past, present and emerging and recognise the strength, resilience and capacity of all Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people. ABN 28 441 859 157 | CRICOS Provider No. 01595D | TEQSA Provider No. PRV12082 Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. By continuing, you agree that you have read our Privacy Statement I do not accept I accept"
