    "https://careers.usc.edu.au/jobs/academic-director-head-of-education-transformation-unisc-sunshine-coast-qld-australia": {
      "title": "Academic Director & Head of Education Transformation",
      "description": "Academic Director & Head of Education Transformation - UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia Contact Us Candidate login Explore Opportunities Academic jobs Professional jobs Casual jobs Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander jobs Recruitment process Employer information Applicant Settings Kiosk mode < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNITIES Academic Director & Head of Education Transformation 90 Sippy Downs Drive, UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia, 4556 Academic Centre for Support and Advancement of Learning and Teaching Director Education design LD $174,423 - $192,092 +17% super Show More Show Less Full-Time Add to favourites View favourites Centre for Learning and Teaching, Sunshine Coast Campus, Sippy Downs Level D, $174,423 - $192,092 p.a., plus up to 17% employer superannuation Full-time, ongoing appointment | 4 days per week on campus The Opportunity The Centre for Learning and Teaching (CLT) provides strategic leadership for learning and teaching excellence across UniSC, partnering with Schools and professional services to enhance educational quality and deliver exceptional student outcomes. Reporting to the Pro Vice-Chancellor (Education), this influential leadership position will drive UniSC's education transformation agenda, shaping the future of curriculum, assessment, academic integrity and teaching innovation across the University. As Academic Director & Head of Education Transformation, you will lead strategic initiatives that strengthen academic quality, build educator capability, and enhance the student learning experience. Working collaboratively with senior academic and professional leaders, you will champion contemporary, evidence-informed educational practices and ensure UniSC remains at the forefront of higher education innovation. This is a career-defining opportunity for a nationally recognised academic leader to influence university-wide transformation while building a culture of teaching excellence, educational scholarship and continuous improvement. For more information on the Centre for Learning and Teaching, please visit us online: Centre for Learning and Teaching You will: lead UniSC’s education transformation agenda, shaping institutional strategy and providing expert advice on learning, teaching, academic quality and governance; drive innovation and quality in education, advancing curriculum design, assessment, academic integrity, teaching practice and continuous improvement frameworks; build capability and foster excellence, leading professional development initiatives, mentoring multidisciplinary teams and cultivating a collaborative, high-performing culture; and strengthen partnerships and future-focused learning, collaborating with schools and stakeholders, representing UniSC in external networks, and leveraging emerging trends in higher education and educational technology to enhance student success and graduate outcomes. About you: You are an accomplished academic leader with a strong reputation for advancing learning and teaching excellence within higher education. Comfortable operating at both strategic and operational levels, you bring the credibility, influence and vision required to lead complex education transformation initiatives and inspire change across a diverse university community. You have a proven ability to build partnerships, influence senior stakeholders and create environments where innovation, collaboration and excellence thrive. Passionate about student success and educational impact, you are motivated by the opportunity to shape the future of learning at an institution committed to transformative education. You will possess: A doctoral qualification in a relevant discipline and substantial experience in senior academic leadership. Demonstrated success leading education transformation, curriculum innovation and assessment enhancement initiatives. A distinguished record of teaching excellence and leadership in learning and teaching. Evidence of leading research-informed approaches that improve educational quality and student outcomes. A strong Scholarship of Learning and Teaching (SoTL) profile, including research outputs, impact and external recognition. Experience mentoring and developing academic capability and fostering cultures of continuous improvement. Extensive experience in academic governance, quality assurance and university administration. Outstanding stakeholder engagement skills and the ability to develop productive regional, national and international partnerships. The capacity to influence institutional strategy and lead change across complex organisational environments. A collaborative and inclusive leadership style that aligns with UniSC's values of integrity, community and sustainability. UniSC is an equal opportunity employer, committed to diversity and inclusion. We encourage applications from all backgrounds, including those with disabilities, women in STEM, First Nations Peoples, and individuals of diverse cultures, genders, abilities, and experiences. We value achievement relative to opportunity and encourage your commentary on your achievements in this context. For additional support during the application process, please contact us at unisc-careers@usc.edu.au or call +61 7 5430 2830. How to apply All applications must be lodged through our website. To apply please visit our website at: Careers at UniSC Applications for this position close midnight, Sunday 27 September 2026 Position description: 494784_Academic Director and Head of Education Transformation.pdf Your completed application must include: a resume, and a response to selection criteria. Noting that within the application form, we will request a statement addressing each of the selection criteria contained within the position description. Further information regarding how to prepare your application is available on our website: Join our team. Have questions or want to know more? For a confidential discussion, please contact: Professor Maree Dinan-Thompson Pro Vice Chancellor (Education) Telephone: 07 5456 3921 Email: pvceducation@usc.edu.au We would love the opportunity to get to know you better, but we know it works both ways. To get to know a little more about us, visit us at: Welcome to UniSC and LinkedIn Life UniSC values a diverse and talented workforce and invites applications from candidates who already have legal work rights in Australia. UniSC does not accept unsolicited applications. For agency inquiries, contact unisc-careers@usc.edu.au Discover UniSC We’re all about doing work that matters, connecting with great people, and being part of an incredible journey. While we’re not the largest university, we are one of the fastest growing in Australia, now with over 2,000 staff across five campuses in South East Queensland and an expanding presence in major capital cities, and we’re making a big impact every day through ground-breaking research, a strong commitment to sustainability, high-performance sport, and award-winning alumni. We are committed to delivering high-quality research and teaching that address major global and regional challenges, with established and emerging strengths in sustainability, environmental systems, biodiversity, aquaculture, preventative health and regional resilience. Our research excellence is internationally recognised through strong performance in global benchmarking, including leading rankings in the 2025 Times Higher Education (THE) Impact Rankings for “Zero Hunger,” “Climate Action” and “Life on Land.” UniSC is also recognised for its teaching excellence, with a strong emphasis on student success, innovative and engaging learning experiences, and strong graduate outcomes that equip learners to make meaningful contributions in their chosen fields. As the only university operating within three UNESCO Biosphere Reserves and a UNESCO World Heritage Site, UniSC is uniquely positioned to leverage its natural environment to advance impactful research, teaching and partnerships that support sustainable futures, with sustainability embedded across all aspects of our teaching, research and operations. We foster a collaborative and supportive environment that encourages continuous professional development and provides the tools and resources to grow your career. We value the contributions of every team member and the role they play in our culture and success. We’re not afraid to do things differently, and we’re looking for people who share our values and want to be part of a team working together to make a meaningful difference to local and global challenges. Our Culture & Benefits: Our collaborative, passionate and welcoming culture is what really sets us apart. Modern teaching & research facilities. Professional development and career pathway opportunities. We are a proud recipient of the prestigious Athena SWAN Bronze Award, granted as part of the Science in Australia Gender Equity (SAGE) initiative. Flexible work arrangements & generous leave options. Salary packing options + 17% Super. EAP, fitness passport & discounted private health. < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNTIES About UniSC For more information about UniSC's employment benefits and culture, including employee blogs, visit our employer information page . Recommended for you Functional Analyst - CRM UniSC Sunshine Coast Individual contributor, L7 $105,843 - $115,703 +17% super, Professional, Student Services, Technical Support Behind every great student experience is a network of systems, processes and people working together seamlessly. As our next Functional Analyst - CRM, you'll play a key role in improving the technology and business processes that help students connect, engage and succeed throughout their journey at UniSC. Technician  (Allied Health - Paramedicine) UniSC Sunshine Coast Academic Support Unit, Individual contributor, L5 $82,843 - $93,358 +17% super, Technical Support Provide technical support and expertise for Paramedicine practical and simulation classes, ensuring smooth delivery, quality learning, and successful student outcomes. Outlets and Operations Officer UniSC Sunshine Coast Campus Development and Services, Individual contributor, L6 $95,986 - $103,873 +17% super Join UniSC as an Outlets Operations Officer and lead the delivery of exceptional food and hospitality services across vibrant campus venues. Clinical Administration Assistant UniSC Sunshine Coast Academic Support Unit, Administration / Admin Support, Individual contributor, L4 $76,275 - $80,218 +17% super Support the delivery of high-quality client services and efficient clinic operations across UniSC's Student-Led Clinics, helping create a professional, welcoming and well-organised environment. LEGAL Privacy Copyright Disclaimer Right to Information Data Collection Preferences The University of the Sunshine Coast acknowledges the Traditional Custodians of the land on which we live, work and study. We pay our respects to local Indigenous Elders past, present and emerging and recognise the strength, resilience and capacity of all Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people. ABN 28 441 859 157 | CRICOS Provider No. 01595D | TEQSA Provider No. PRV12082 Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. By continuing, you agree that you have read our Privacy Statement I do not accept I accept"
