    "https://careers.usc.edu.au/jobs/outlets-and-operations-officer-unisc-sunshine-coast-qld-australia-2e361251-23e2-4d29-800e-91fbe27b1f90": {
      "title": "Outlets and Operations Officer",
      "description": "Outlets and Operations Officer - UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia Contact Us Candidate login Explore Opportunities Academic jobs Professional jobs Casual jobs Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander jobs Recruitment process Employer information Applicant Settings Kiosk mode < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNITIES Outlets and Operations Officer 90 Sippy Downs Drive, UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia, 4556 Campus Development and Services Individual contributor L6 $95,986 - $103,873 +17% super Full-Time Add to favourites View favourites Campus Development and Services | UniSC Sunshine Coast, Sippy Downs Professional Level 6, $95,986 - $103,873 p.a. plus up to 17% employer superannuation Full time, ongoing appointment The Opportunity Venues and Catering at UniSC forms an integral part of Facilities Management, delivering high-quality hospitality services that enhance campus life for students, staff, and visitors. As part of this dynamic and customer-focused team, the Outlets Operations Officer will play a pivotal role in shaping the future of UniSC’s on-campus food services. You’ll be joining a forward-thinking unit committed to excellence in service, innovation in delivery, and a seamless campus experience. In this role, you’ll be responsible for the day-to-day operations of UniSC-owned catering outlets, working closely with the Venues and Catering Manager to deliver outstanding service across multiple sites. Your expertise will ensure efficient operations, a safe and positive working environment, and customer-focused offerings aligned with evolving food and beverage trends. You will supervise and coordinate daily operations across UniSC food outlets to ensure consistency, quality, and compliance with food safety standards; contribute to the planning and successful delivery of outlet refurbishment and development projects across UniSC campuses; collaborate with kitchen and service teams on seasonal menu development, staff rostering, and customer engagement strategies; and implement operational improvements that enhance profitability, service delivery, and team performance. About you You are a proactive and experienced hospitality professional who thrives in fast-paced environments and takes pride in delivering exceptional service. With a strong background in food outlet management, you understand what it takes to lead teams, oversee multiple venues, and ensure the smooth, profitable operation of hospitality services. Collaborative and solutions-focused, you bring operational insight, creativity, and a commitment to excellence in every aspect of your work. You will possess: a degree in hospitality or related field with relevant experience, or an equivalent combination of leadership experience and education/training; demonstrated ability to manage food service operations, including staff supervision, budgeting, and compliance with WHS, food safety, and liquor licensing regulations; strong communication and interpersonal skills to effectively liaise with a range of stakeholders; experience overseeing or contributing to the design and planning of refurbishment or construction projects in hospitality settings; the ability to work independently, meet operational deadlines, and manage multiple priorities across outlets and campuses; and a passion for delivering high-quality, customer-focused food and beverage experiences that enhance campus life. Don't meet every requirement? At UniSC, we understand that your work and life experiences can be just as valuable. If you're excited about this role but your CV doesn't align perfectly with our position description, we encourage you to apply anyway. You may be just the right candidate for this or one of our many other opportunities. UniSC is an equal opportunity employer, committed to diversity and inclusion. We encourage applications from all backgrounds, including those with disabilities, women in STEM, First Nations Peoples, and individuals of diverse cultures, genders, abilities, and experiences. We value achievement relative to opportunity and encourage your commentary on your achievements in this context. For additional support during the application process, please contact us at unisc-careers@usc.edu.au or call +61 7 5430 2830. How to apply All applications must be lodged through our website. To apply please visit our website at: Careers at UniSC Applications for this position close midnight, Sunday 27 September 2026 Position Description: 494815_Outlets and Operations Officer.pdf Your completed application must include: a resume and a statement of suitability (not to exceed two pages), which will be reviewed in alignment to the specified selection criteria as outlined within the position description. Further information regarding how to prepare your application is available on our website: Join our team. Have questions or want to know more? For a confidential discussion, please contact: Ursula Dodds Venues and Catering Manager – Venues and Catering Telephone: 07 5459 4565 Email: udodds@usc.edu.au We would love the opportunity to get to know you better, but we know it works both ways. To get to know a little more about us, visit us at: Welcome to UniSC and LinkedIn Life UniSC values a diverse and talented workforce and invites applications from candidates who already have legal work rights in Australia. UniSC does not accept unsolicited applications. For agency inquiries, contact unisc-careers@usc.edu.au Discover UniSC We’re all about doing work that matters, connecting with great people, and being part of an incredible journey. While we’re not the largest university, we are one of the fastest growing in Australia, now with over 2,000 staff across five campuses in South East Queensland and an expanding presence in major capital cities, and we’re making a big impact every day through ground-breaking research, a strong commitment to sustainability, high-performance sport, and award-winning alumni. We are committed to delivering high-quality research and teaching that address major global and regional challenges, with established and emerging strengths in sustainability, environmental systems, biodiversity, aquaculture, preventative health and regional resilience. Our research excellence is internationally recognised through strong performance in global benchmarking, including leading rankings in the 2025 Times Higher Education (THE) Impact Rankings for “Zero Hunger,” “Climate Action” and “Life on Land.” UniSC is also recognised for its teaching excellence, with a strong emphasis on student success, innovative and engaging learning experiences, and strong graduate outcomes that equip learners to make meaningful contributions in their chosen fields. As the only university operating within three UNESCO Biosphere Reserves and a UNESCO World Heritage Site, UniSC is uniquely positioned to leverage its natural environment to advance impactful research, teaching and partnerships that support sustainable futures, with sustainability embedded across all aspects of our teaching, research and operations. We foster a collaborative and supportive environment that encourages continuous professional development and provides the tools and resources to grow your career. We value the contributions of every team member and the role they play in our culture and success. We’re not afraid to do things differently, and we’re looking for people who share our values and want to be part of a team working together to make a meaningful difference to local and global challenges. Our Culture & Benefits: Our collaborative, passionate and welcoming culture is what really sets us apart. Modern teaching & research facilities. Professional development and career pathway opportunities. We are a proud recipient of the prestigious Athena SWAN Bronze Award, granted as part of the Science in Australia Gender Equity (SAGE) initiative. Flexible work arrangements & generous leave options. Salary packing options + 17% Super. EAP, fitness passport & discounted private health. Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:47 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:47 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles subtitles settings , opens subtitles settings dialog subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNTIES Apply now! Enter your details below to commence your application: First Name (required) 7980e085 Last Name (required) 1cf54ff5 Email (required) 3b382d5e Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you About UniSC For more information about UniSC's employment benefits and culture, including employee blogs, visit our employer information page . Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 3:17 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 3:17 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles subtitles settings , opens subtitles settings dialog subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of di