    "https://careers.usc.edu.au/jobs/technician-nursing-and-midwifery-unisc-moreton-bay-queensland-australia-unisc-caboolture-qld-unisc-gympie-unisc-fraser-coast": {
      "title": "Technician (Nursing and Midwifery)",
      "description": "Technician (Nursing and Midwifery) - UniSC Moreton Bay, Queensland, Australia - UniSC Caboolture, QLD, Australia - UniSC Gympie, QLD, Australia - UniSC Fraser Coast, QLD, Australia Contact Us Candidate login Explore Opportunities Academic jobs Professional jobs Casual jobs Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander jobs Recruitment process Employer information Applicant Settings Kiosk mode < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNITIES Technician (Nursing and Midwifery) UniSC Caboolture, QLD, Australia, 4510 161-179 Old Maryborough Road, UniSC Fraser Coast, QLD, Australia, 4655 71 Cartwright Road, UniSC Gympie, QLD, Australia, 4570 1 Moreton Parade, UniSC Moreton Bay, Queensland, Australia, 4502 Show More Show Less Academic Support Unit L5 $82,843 - $93,358 +17% super Technical Support Full-Time Part-Time Add to favourites View favourites Academic Support Unit | UniSC Moreton Bay, UniSC Caboolture, UniSC Gympie and UniSC Fraser Coast Level 5, $82,843 - $93,358 p.a. full-time equivalent, plus up to 17% employer superannuation Multiple newly created positions available: Moreton Bay: Part-time (29 hours per week), ongoing Caboolture: Full-time (36.25 hours per week), ongoing and part-time (80% FTE, 29 hours per week), ongoing Gympie: Part-time (21.75 hours per week), ongoing Fraser Coast: Part-time (21.75 hours per week), ongoing The Opportunity Join a growing team supporting the expansion of UniSC’s Nursing and Midwifery programs. These newly created positions have been established in response to continued growth across the University and increasing demand for Nursing and Midwifery education. You will provide specialist technical support across clinical teaching and high-fidelity simulation environments, ensuring facilities, equipment and resources are safe, well-prepared and ready to support high-quality learning experiences. Bring your clinical or technical expertise into a university environment and play an important role in supporting the next generation of Nursing and Midwifery professionals. Working closely with academic and professional staff, you will prepare and maintain clinical learning environments, operate simulation technologies and provide practical technical support that enables effective student learning. Please note: This role provides technical and simulation support and does not undertake teaching, assessment, or student instruction responsibilities. You will provide technical expertise and support for undergraduate and postgraduate Nursing and Midwifery programs, including preparing and facilitating high-fidelity simulation and clinical learning environments; prepare, maintain and safely operate clinical equipment, simulation technologies, facilities and resources, working closely with academic staff to ensure environments are safe, functional and ready for scheduled learning activities; and provide technical guidance and problem-solving support, including training staff in the use of simulation equipment and, where required, training and supervising casual team members. About you You bring strong interpersonal skills and communicate effectively across verbal, written and active listening contexts. You work confidently both independently and within a team, showing initiative and adapting readily to change and new situations. Proactive and self-directed, you manage high-volume workloads with minimal supervision while applying strong analytical and problem-solving skills to deliver practical, effective outcomes. You will possess: Completion of a relevant degree, or a combination of relevant experience and education/training may also be considered, with experience providing technical and practical support within a tertiary educational, clinical or similar environment. Experience supporting Nursing and Midwifery disciplines would be desirable; Demonstrated experience providing practical and technical support in a teaching, workshop, clinical or similar environment, with the ability to prepare and facilitate high-quality practical and simulated learning experiences; A demonstrated commitment to utilising simulation methodology in learning and its ability to transform education, with the ability and willingness to learn and support new technologies and techniques; Sound knowledge of workplace health and safety practices, including experience conducting and documenting risk assessments, implementing safe operating procedures, and working in accordance with relevant policies, guidelines and legislation; Strong organisational and time management skills, with the ability to work independently, manage competing priorities, meet deadlines and adapt to changing requirements in a high-volume environment; and Effective communication, interpersonal, analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to work collaboratively with academic, technical and professional staff and students, build positive working relationships, and provide accurate and timely advice. Don't meet every requirement? At UniSC, we understand that your work and life experiences can be just as valuable. If you're excited about this role but your CV doesn't align perfectly with our position description, we encourage you to apply anyway. You may be just the right candidate for this or one of our many other opportunities. UniSC is an equal opportunity employer, committed to diversity and inclusion. We encourage applications from all backgrounds, including those with disabilities, women in STEM, First Nations Peoples, and individuals of diverse cultures, genders, abilities, and experiences. We value achievement relative to opportunity and encourage your commentary on your achievements in this context. For additional support during the application process, please contact us at unisc-careers@usc.edu.au or call +61 7 5430 2830. How to apply All applications must be lodged through our website. To apply please visit our website at: Careers at UniSC Applications for this position close midnight, Sunday 27 September 2026. Position Description: 494829_Technician (Nursing and Midwifery).pdf Your completed application must include: a resume and a statement of suitability (not to exceed two pages), which will be reviewed in alignment to the specified selection criteria as outlined within the position description. Further information regarding how to prepare your application is available on our website: Join our team. Have questions or want to know more? For a confidential discussion, please contact: Suzy O'Brien Team Leader, Nursing and Midwifery - Academic Support Unit Telephone: 07 5456 5368 Email: sobrien2@usc.edu.au We would love the opportunity to get to know you better, but we know it works both ways. To get to know a little more about us, visit us at: Welcome to UniSC and LinkedIn Life UniSC values a diverse and talented workforce and invites applications from candidates who already have legal work rights in Australia. UniSC does not accept unsolicited applications. For agency inquiries, contact unisc-careers@usc.edu.au Discover UniSC We’re all about doing work that matters, connecting with great people, and being part of an incredible journey. While we’re not the largest university, we are one of the fastest growing in Australia, now with over 2,000 staff across five campuses in South East Queensland and an expanding presence in major capital cities, and we’re making a big impact every day through ground-breaking research, a strong commitment to sustainability, high-performance sport, and award-winning alumni. We are committed to delivering high-quality research and teaching that address major global and regional challenges, with established and emerging strengths in sustainability, environmental systems, biodiversity, aquaculture, preventative health and regional resilience. Our research excellence is internationally recognised through strong performance in global benchmarking, including leading rankings in the 2025 Times Higher Education (THE) Impact Rankings for “Zero Hunger,” “Climate Action” and “Life on Land.” UniSC is also recognised for its teaching excellence, with a strong emphasis on student success, innovative and engaging learning experiences, and strong graduate outcomes that equip learners to make meaningful contributions in their chosen fields. As the only university operating within three UNESCO Biosphere Reserves and a UNESCO World Heritage Site, UniSC is uniquely positioned to leverage its natural environment to advance impactful research, teaching and partnerships that support sustainable futures, with sustainability embedded across all aspects of our teaching, research and operations. We foster a collaborative and supportive environment that encourages continuous professional development and provides the tools and resources to grow your career. We value the contributions of every team member and the role they play in our culture and success. We’re not afraid to do things differently, and we’re looking for people who share our values and want to be part of a team working together to make a meaningful difference to local and global challenges. Our Culture & Benefits: Our collaborative, passionate and welcoming culture is what really sets us apart. Modern teaching & research facilities. Professional development and career pathway opportunities. We are a proud recipient of the prestigious Athena SWAN Bronze Award, granted as part of the Science in Australia Gender Equity (SAGE) initiative. Flexible work arrangements & generous leave options. Salary packing options + 17% Super. EAP, fitness passport & discounted private health. < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNTIES About UniSC For more information about UniSC's employment benefits and culture, including employee blogs, visit our employer information page . Recommended for you Functional Analyst - CRM UniSC Sunshine Coast Individual contributor, L7 $105,843 - $115,703 +17% super, Professional, Student Services, Technical Support Behind every great student experience is a network of systems, processes and people working together seamlessly. As our next Functional Analyst - CRM, you'll play a key role in improving the technology and business processes that help students connect, engage and succeed throughout their journey at UniSC. Technician  (Allied Health - Paramedicine) UniSC Sunshine Coast Academic Support Unit, Individual contributor, L5 $82,843 - $93,358 +17% super, Technical Support Provide technical support and expertise for Paramedicine practical and simulation classes, ensuring smooth delivery, quality learning, and successful student outcomes. Outlets and Operations Officer UniSC Sunshine Coast Campus Development and Services, Individual contributor, L6 $95,986 - $103,873 +17% super Join UniSC as an Outlets Operations Officer and lead the delivery of exceptional food and hospitality services across vibrant campus venues. Clinical Administration Assistant UniSC Sunshine Coast Academic Support Unit, Administration / Admin Support, Individual contributor, L4 $76,275 - $80,218 +17% super Support the delivery of high-quality client services and efficient clinic operations across UniSC's Student-Led Clinics, helping create a professional, welcoming and well-organised environment. LEGAL Privacy Copyright Disclaimer Right to Information Data Collection Preferences The University of the Sunshine Coast acknowledges the Traditional Custodians of the land on which we live, work and study. We pay our respects to local Indigenous Elders past, present and emerging and recognise the strength, resilience and capacity of all Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people. ABN 28 441 859 157 | CRICOS Provider No. 01595D | TEQSA Provider No. PRV12082 Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. By continuing, you agree that you have read our Privacy Statement I do not accept I accept"
