    "https://careers.usc.edu.au/jobs/work-integrated-learning-wil-placement-officer-unisc-moreton-bay-queensland-australia": {
      "title": "Work Integrated Learning (WIL) Placement Officer",
      "description": "Work Integrated Learning (WIL) Placement Officer - UniSC Moreton Bay, Queensland, Australia Contact Us Candidate login Explore Opportunities Academic jobs Professional jobs Casual jobs Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander jobs Recruitment process Employer information Applicant Settings Kiosk mode < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNITIES Work Integrated Learning (WIL) Placement Officer 1 Moreton Parade, UniSC Moreton Bay, Queensland, Australia, 4502 Academic Support Unit Administration / Admin Support Individual contributor L5 $82,843 - $93,358 +17% super Professional Show More Show Less Full-Time Add to favourites View favourites Academic Support Unit | UniSC Moreton Bay, Petrie Level 5 $82,843 - $93,358 p.a., plus up to 17% employer superannuation Full-time, ongoing appointment The Opportunity The Work Integrated Learning (WIL) team, within UniSC’s Academic Support Unit, plays a vital role in connecting students with meaningful industry placement experiences that enhance their employability and professional development. Providing specialist support across undergraduate, postgraduate and higher degree by research programs, the team ensures placement activities meet university requirements, regulatory obligations and industry expectations. You will play a key role in connecting students with high-quality placement experiences that enhance their learning and prepare them for professional success. Providing specialist operational and administrative support across a diverse portfolio of placements, you will independently coordinate placement activities, offer expert advice on placement requirements, maintain critical systems and records, and build strong relationships with host organisations, academics and internal stakeholders. Your work will directly contribute to expanding and enhancing work-integrated learning opportunities and ensuring students and partners are supported throughout every stage of the placement journey, in alignment with UniSC’s strategic priorities. You will Provide high-quality, timely and accurate administrative and operational services supporting the University's Work Integrated Learning (WIL) courses and student placements; Develop and maintain effective relationships with students, academic and professional staff, and external host organisations to facilitate suitable, safe and successful WIL experiences; and Apply WIL knowledge, University policies and procedures to resolve operational issues and contribute to the continuous improvement of WIL systems, processes and services. About you You are a highly organised and customer-focused professional who enjoys working in a fast-paced environment where no two days are the same. You bring strong administrative capability, excellent stakeholder relationship skills and the ability to navigate complex processes while maintaining a focus on service excellence. You are proactive, solutions-focused and committed to creating positive outcomes for students and industry partners alike. You will possess: Completion of an advanced diploma, combined with at least 4 years subsequent relevant experience, or an equivalent experience and/or education/training; Well-developed organisational and administrative skills, with the ability to independently plan and prioritise work, coordinate competing requirements and meet deadlines in a dynamic environment; Demonstrated customer service skills and a results-oriented approach, with the ability to provide timely and appropriate advice to diverse stakeholders; Well-developed attention to detail, data entry, communication and reporting skills, including proficiency in the University's Placement Management System and other relevant technologies; Well-developed written, oral and interpersonal communication skills, with the ability to build effective relationships and collaborate with students, academic and professional staff, and external host organisations; Demonstrated ability to work independently under general direction, exercise initiative and sound judgement, interpret and apply policies and procedures, resolve problems and make appropriate decisions, escalating matters where required; Demonstrated ability to apply established policies and procedures and contribute to the continuous improvement of work processes, systems and documentation; and Demonstrated knowledge of Work Integrated Learning in the higher education sector, including relevant University policies, procedures and regulatory and accreditation requirements. Don't meet every requirement? At UniSC, we understand that your work and life experiences can be just as valuable. If you're excited about this role but your CV doesn't align perfectly with our position description, we encourage you to apply anyway. You may be just the right candidate for this or one of our many other opportunities. UniSC is an equal opportunity employer, committed to diversity and inclusion. We encourage applications from all backgrounds, including those with disabilities, women in STEM, First Nations Peoples, and individuals of diverse cultures, genders, abilities, and experiences. We value achievement relative to opportunity and encourage your commentary on your achievements in this context. For additional support during the application process, please contact us at unisc-careers@usc.edu.au or call +61 7 5430 2830. How to apply All applications must be lodged through our website. To apply please visit our website at: Careers at UniSC Applications for this position close midnight, Sunday 20 September 2026. Position description: 494831_Work Integrated Learning (WIL) Placement Officer.pdf Your completed application must include: a resume and a statement of suitability (not to exceed two pages), which will be reviewed in alignment to the specified selection criteria as outlined within the position description. Further information regarding how to prepare your application is available on our website: Join our team. Have questions or want to know more? For a confidential discussion, please contact: Dannielle Cochrane Team Leader, WIL Systems and Compliance Telephone: 07 5456 3415 Email: dcochran@usc.edu.au We would love the opportunity to get to know you better, but we know it works both ways. To get to know a little more about us, visit us at: Welcome to UniSC and LinkedIn Life UniSC values a diverse and talented workforce and invites applications from candidates who already have legal work rights in Australia. UniSC does not accept unsolicited applications. For agency inquiries, contact unisc-careers@usc.edu.au Discover UniSC We’re all about doing work that matters, connecting with great people, and being part of an incredible journey. While we’re not the largest university, we are one of the fastest growing in Australia, now with over 2,000 staff across five campuses in South East Queensland and an expanding presence in major capital cities, and we’re making a big impact every day through ground-breaking research, a strong commitment to sustainability, high-performance sport, and award-winning alumni. We are committed to delivering high-quality research and teaching that address major global and regional challenges, with established and emerging strengths in sustainability, environmental systems, biodiversity, aquaculture, preventative health and regional resilience. Our research excellence is internationally recognised through strong performance in global benchmarking, including leading rankings in the 2025 Times Higher Education (THE) Impact Rankings for “Zero Hunger,” “Climate Action” and “Life on Land.” UniSC is also recognised for its teaching excellence, with a strong emphasis on student success, innovative and engaging learning experiences, and strong graduate outcomes that equip learners to make meaningful contributions in their chosen fields. As the only university operating within three UNESCO Biosphere Reserves and a UNESCO World Heritage Site, UniSC is uniquely positioned to leverage its natural environment to advance impactful research, teaching and partnerships that support sustainable futures, with sustainability embedded across all aspects of our teaching, research and operations. We foster a collaborative and supportive environment that encourages continuous professional development and provides the tools and resources to grow your career. We value the contributions of every team member and the role they play in our culture and success. We’re not afraid to do things differently, and we’re looking for people who share our values and want to be part of a team working together to make a meaningful difference to local and global challenges. Our Culture & Benefits: Our collaborative, passionate and welcoming culture is what really sets us apart. Modern teaching & research facilities. Professional development and career pathway opportunities. We are a proud recipient of the prestigious Athena SWAN Bronze Award, granted as part of the Science in Australia Gender Equity (SAGE) initiative. Flexible work arrangements & generous leave options. Salary packing options + 17% Super. EAP, fitness passport & discounted private health. Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:47 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:47 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles subtitles settings , opens subtitles settings dialog subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75