    "https://careers.usc.edu.au/jobs/project-manager-business-short-courses-unisc-sunshine-coast-qld-australia": {
      "title": "Project Manager, Business Short Courses",
      "description": "Project Manager, Business Short Courses - UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia Contact Us Candidate login Explore Opportunities Academic jobs Professional jobs Casual jobs Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander jobs Recruitment process Employer information Applicant Settings Kiosk mode < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNITIES Project Manager, Business Short Courses 90 Sippy Downs Drive, UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia, 4556 L9 $138,698 - $145,268 +17% super Professional Project Management School of Business and Creative Industries Show More Show Less Full-Time Add to favourites View favourites School of Business and Creative Industries, Sunshine Coast Campus, Sippy Downs Level 9, $138,698 - $145,268 p.a., plus up to 17% employer superannuation Full-time, fixed-term until 30 June 2029 The Opportunity Join UniSC and play a pivotal role in delivering an established and growing government-funded business short courses project that supports businesses across Queensland. Working within the School of Business and Creative Industries, this role is responsible for the operational leadership, performance, and continuous improvement of a large-scale learning initiative designed to strengthen business planning capability and long-term sustainability. You will oversee the planning, delivery, governance and ongoing enhancement of a complex, externally funded program. You will bring together academic expertise, industry engagement, educational technology and operational excellence to ensure courses are delivered to the highest standard while meeting university and government requirements. This is an opportunity to shape a flagship program with meaningful impact, leading a multidisciplinary team and building strong partnerships with government, industry and university stakeholders. Your work will directly contribute to strengthening workforce capability, business resilience and economic sustainability across Queensland communities. You will lead the end-to-end delivery, performance and continuous improvement of a statewide business short courses project, ensuring quality outcomes for participants and stakeholders; build and lead a high-performing team while overseeing course delivery, educational technologies, resource planning and operational excellence across multiple cohorts and locations; develop strong partnerships with government, industry and university stakeholders, providing strategic advice, governance, reporting and risk management to support program success; and manage budgets, systems and performance frameworks, using data and stakeholder insights to drive innovation, accountability and long-term sustainability. About you You are a strategic and delivery-focused leader who thrives in complex environments and enjoys bringing people together to achieve meaningful outcomes. You combine strong project management expertise with exceptional stakeholder engagement skills and have a track record of delivering high-quality learning, training or professional development programs at scale. You are equally comfortable leading teams, managing operational priorities, navigating governance requirements and identifying opportunities for innovation and improvement. Most importantly, you are motivated by creating impact through education and partnership. You will possess: Demonstrated experience delivering high-quality blended or HyFlex learning programs across multiple locations and cohorts. Strong expertise in project governance, risk management and operational improvement. Proven ability to lead multidisciplinary teams and build productive relationships with academic, industry and government stakeholders. Experience using educational technologies and learning management systems to support engaging learning outcomes. Outstanding written and verbal communication skills, including experience preparing high-level reports and project documentation. Financial and workforce management capability, including budget oversight and resource planning. Strong judgement, problem-solving skills and the ability to manage competing priorities in a dynamic environment Don't meet every requirement? At UniSC, we understand that your work and life experiences can be just as valuable. If you're excited about this role but your CV doesn't align perfectly with our position description, we encourage you to apply anyway. You may be just the right candidate for this or one of our many other opportunities. UniSC is an equal opportunity employer, committed to diversity and inclusion. We encourage applications from all backgrounds, including those with disabilities, women in STEM, First Nations Peoples, and individuals of diverse cultures, genders, abilities, and experiences. We value achievement relative to opportunity and encourage your commentary on your achievements in this context. For additional support during the application process, please contact us at unisc-careers@usc.edu.au or call +61 7 5430 2830. How to apply All applications must be lodged through our website. To apply please visit our website at: Careers at UniSC Applications for this position close midnight, Sunday 20 September 2026 Position description: 494807_Project Manager.pdf Your completed application must include: a resume, and responses to specific pre-determined selection criteria as outlined in the application form. Further information regarding how to prepare your application is available on our website: Join our team. Have questions or want to know more? For a confidential discussion, please contact: Wayne Graham Senior Lecturer in Management Telephone: 07 5430 1287 Email: wgraham@usc.edu.au We would love the opportunity to get to know you better, but we know it works both ways. To get to know a little more about us, visit us at: Welcome to UniSC and LinkedIn Life UniSC values a diverse and talented workforce and invites applications from candidates who already have legal work rights in Australia. UniSC does not accept unsolicited applications. For agency inquiries, contact unisc-careers@usc.edu.au Discover UniSC We’re all about doing work that matters, connecting with great people, and being part of an incredible journey. While we’re not the largest university, we are one of the fastest growing in Australia, now with over 2,000 staff across five campuses in South East Queensland and an expanding presence in major capital cities, and we’re making a big impact every day through ground-breaking research, a strong commitment to sustainability, high-performance sport, and award-winning alumni. We are committed to delivering high-quality research and teaching that address major global and regional challenges, with established and emerging strengths in sustainability, environmental systems, biodiversity, aquaculture, preventative health and regional resilience. Our research excellence is internationally recognised through strong performance in global benchmarking, including leading rankings in the 2025 Times Higher Education (THE) Impact Rankings for “Zero Hunger,” “Climate Action” and “Life on Land.” UniSC is also recognised for its teaching excellence, with a strong emphasis on student success, innovative and engaging learning experiences, and strong graduate outcomes that equip learners to make meaningful contributions in their chosen fields. As the only university operating within three UNESCO Biosphere Reserves and a UNESCO World Heritage Site, UniSC is uniquely positioned to leverage its natural environment to advance impactful research, teaching and partnerships that support sustainable futures, with sustainability embedded across all aspects of our teaching, research and operations. We foster a collaborative and supportive environment that encourages continuous professional development and provides the tools and resources to grow your career. We value the contributions of every team member and the role they play in our culture and success. We’re not afraid to do things differently, and we’re looking for people who share our values and want to be part of a team working together to make a meaningful difference to local and global challenges. Our Culture & Benefits: Our collaborative, passionate and welcoming culture is what really sets us apart. Modern teaching & research facilities. Professional development and career pathway opportunities. We are a proud recipient of the prestigious Athena SWAN Bronze Award, granted as part of the Science in Australia Gender Equity (SAGE) initiative. Flexible work arrangements & generous leave options. Salary packing options + 17% Super. EAP, fitness passport & discounted private health. Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:47 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:47 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles subtitles settings , opens subtitles settings dialog subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNTIES Apply now! Enter your details below to commence your application: First Name (required) 00efaa0e Last Name (required) c4624a7c Email (required) e5d0645f Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you 