    "https://careers.usc.edu.au/jobs/project-coordinator-unisc-sunshine-coast-qld-australia": {
      "title": "Project Coordinator",
      "description": "Project Coordinator - UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia Contact Us Candidate login Explore Opportunities Academic jobs Professional jobs Casual jobs Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander jobs Recruitment process Employer information Applicant Settings Kiosk mode < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNITIES Project Coordinator 90 Sippy Downs Drive, UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia, 4556 Individual contributor L6 $95,986 - $103,873 +17% super School of Business and Creative Industries Full-Time Add to favourites View favourites School of Business and Creative Industries | UniSC Sunshine Coast, Sippy Downs Level 6, $95,986 - $103,873 p.a., plus up to 17% employer superannuation Full-time (36.25 hours per week), fixed term appointment until June 2029 The Opportunity The School of Business and Creative Industries is seeking an organised and collaborative Project Coordinator to support the delivery of a four-year Queensland Government-funded project supporting the Queensland business community. The project delivers a suite of non-credit bearing business short courses designed to build business capability and support long-term sustainability through the development, application and implementation of practical planning tools. Building on six years of successful course delivery and ongoing refinement, the project is entering its next phase of delivery and continued impact. In this role, you will coordinate participant-facing operations across multiple courses and cohorts, working closely with academic and professional staff, facilitators, government and industry stakeholders to support high-quality, accessible and engaging learning experiences. For more information, please visit us online: School of Business and Creative Industries You will coordinate the planning, implementation and ongoing delivery of micro-credential courses, ensuring activities, timelines and participant processes are effectively managed; work collaboratively with academic staff, facilitators, government and industry stakeholders to support course delivery, participant engagement and project outcomes; and oversee learning systems, course communications, resources and evaluation activities, using participant and project data to identify opportunities for continuous improvement. About you You are an organised, proactive and collaborative project professional with experience coordinating educational programs, projects or initiatives in a university or similar environment. You bring strong organisational and digital skills, with the ability to manage competing priorities, coordinate multiple activities and maintain attention to detail. You are a confident communicator who can build productive relationships with diverse stakeholders and use initiative and sound judgement to resolve issues and improve processes. Experience with micro-credentials, short courses, learning management systems or government-funded programs will be highly regarded. You will possess: A relevant degree and demonstrated experience in project coordination, program administration or a related field; Demonstrated experience coordinating and delivering micro-credentials, short courses, educational programs or similar initiatives in a tertiary or comparable environment; Strong communication, interpersonal and stakeholder engagement skills, including the ability to work effectively with academic, industry, government and diverse participant groups; Well-developed digital and learning systems capabilities, including experience with learning management systems such as Canvas and participant or enrolment processes; Excellent organisational, planning and prioritisation skills, with the ability to manage competing demands, coordinate multiple activities and deliver within deadlines; and Demonstrated initiative, sound judgement and problem-solving skills, including the ability to interpret information, develop practical recommendations and contribute to continuous improvement in a complex environment. Don't meet every requirement? At UniSC, we understand that your work and life experiences can be just as valuable. If you're excited about this role but your CV doesn't align perfectly with our position description, we encourage you to apply anyway. You may be just the right candidate for this or one of our many other opportunities. UniSC is an equal opportunity employer, committed to diversity and inclusion. We encourage applications from all backgrounds, including those with disabilities, women in STEM, First Nations Peoples, and individuals of diverse cultures, genders, abilities, and experiences. We value achievement relative to opportunity and encourage your commentary on your achievements in this context. For additional support during the application process, please contact us at unisc-careers@usc.edu.au or call +61 7 5430 2830. How to apply All applications must be lodged through our website. To apply please visit our website at: Careers at UniSC Applications for this position close midnight, Sunday 4 October 2026. Position description: 494865_Project Coordinator.pdf Your completed application must include: a resume and a statement of suitability (not to exceed two pages), which be reviewed in alignment to the specified selection criteria as outlined within the position description. Further information regarding how to prepare your application is available on our website: Join our team. Have questions or want to know more? For a confidential discussion, please contact: Wayne Graham Senior Lecturer in Management Telephone: 07 5430 1287 Email: wgraham@usc.edu.au We would love the opportunity to get to know you better, but we know it works both ways. To get to know a little more about us, visit us at: Welcome to UniSC and LinkedIn Life UniSC values a diverse and talented workforce and invites applications from candidates who already have legal work rights in Australia. UniSC does not accept unsolicited applications. For agency inquiries, contact unisc-careers@usc.edu.au Discover UniSC We’re all about doing work that matters, connecting with great people, and being part of an incredible journey. While we’re not the largest university, we are one of the fastest growing in Australia, now with over 2,000 staff across five campuses in South East Queensland and an expanding presence in major capital cities, and we’re making a big impact every day through ground-breaking research, a strong commitment to sustainability, high-performance sport, and award-winning alumni. We are committed to delivering high-quality research and teaching that address major global and regional challenges, with established and emerging strengths in sustainability, environmental systems, biodiversity, aquaculture, preventative health and regional resilience. Our research excellence is internationally recognised through strong performance in global benchmarking, including leading rankings in the 2025 Times Higher Education (THE) Impact Rankings for “Zero Hunger,” “Climate Action” and “Life on Land.” UniSC is also recognised for its teaching excellence, with a strong emphasis on student success, innovative and engaging learning experiences, and strong graduate outcomes that equip learners to make meaningful contributions in their chosen fields. As the only university operating within three UNESCO Biosphere Reserves and a UNESCO World Heritage Site, UniSC is uniquely positioned to leverage its natural environment to advance impactful research, teaching and partnerships that support sustainable futures, with sustainability embedded across all aspects of our teaching, research and operations. We foster a collaborative and supportive environment that encourages continuous professional development and provides the tools and resources to grow your career. We value the contributions of every team member and the role they play in our culture and success. We’re not afraid to do things differently, and we’re looking for people who share our values and want to be part of a team working together to make a meaningful difference to local and global challenges. Our Culture & Benefits: Our collaborative, passionate and welcoming culture is what really sets us apart. Modern teaching & research facilities. Professional development and career pathway opportunities. We are a proud recipient of the prestigious Athena SWAN Bronze Award, granted as part of the Science in Australia Gender Equity (SAGE) initiative. Flexible work arrangements & generous leave options. Salary packing options + 17% Super. EAP, fitness passport & discounted private health. < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNTIES About UniSC For more information about UniSC's employment benefits and culture, including employee blogs, visit our employer information page . Recommended for you Print Production Officer UniSC Sunshine Coast Individual contributor, L4 $76,275 - $80,218 +17% super, Print Services, Professional Bring ideas to life through quality print, signage and production services that support teaching, learning and research across UniSC. Project Support Officer UniSC Sunshine Coast Administration / Admin Support, Individual contributor, L5 $82,843 - $93,358 +17% super, School of Business and Creative Industries Join UniSC and support the delivery of a Queensland Government-funded initiative that helps Queensland businesses build capability through practical learning. Functional Analyst - CRM UniSC Sunshine Coast Individual contributor, L7 $105,843 - $115,703 +17% super, Professional, Student Services, Technical Support Behind every great student experience is a network of systems, processes and people working together seamlessly. As our next Functional Analyst - CRM, you'll play a key role in improving the technology and business processes that help students connect, engage and succeed throughout their journey at UniSC. Technician  (Allied Health - Paramedicine) UniSC Sunshine Coast Academic Support Unit, Individual contributor, L5 $82,843 - $93,358 +17% super, Technical Support Provide technical support and expertise for Paramedicine practical and simulation classes, ensuring smooth delivery, quality learning, and successful student outcomes. LEGAL Privacy Copyright Disclaimer Right to Information Data Collection Preferences The University of the Sunshine Coast acknowledges the Traditional Custodians of the land on which we live, work and study. We pay our respects to local Indigenous Elders past, present and emerging and recognise the strength, resilience and capacity of all Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people. ABN 28 441 859 157 | CRICOS Provider No. 01595D | TEQSA Provider No. PRV12082 Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. By continuing, you agree that you have read our Privacy Statement I do not accept I accept"
