    "https://careers.usc.edu.au/jobs/print-production-officer-unisc-sunshine-coast-qld-australia": {
      "title": "Print Production Officer",
      "description": "Print Production Officer - UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia Contact Us Candidate login Explore Opportunities Academic jobs Professional jobs Casual jobs Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander jobs Recruitment process Employer information Applicant Settings Kiosk mode < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNITIES Print Production Officer 90 Sippy Downs Drive, UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia, 4556 Individual contributor L4 $76,275 - $80,218 +17% super Print Services Professional Show More Show Less Full-Time Add to favourites View favourites Print Services | UniSC Sunshine Coast, Sippy Downs Level 4, $76,275 - $80,218 p.a., plus up to 17% employer superannuation Full time (36.25 hours per week), ongoing appointment The Opportunity UniSC’s Print Services team plays an important role in supporting students, staff and the broader community by delivering high-quality print production, signage, merchandise and specialist printing solutions across multiple campuses. The team also manages the University’s self-service printing environment, multifunction device fleet and technical print support services. In this role, you will coordinate and deliver expert print production services across digital, wide-format and finishing operations. You will oversee the setup, operation and maintenance of advanced print equipment, ensure consistently high-quality outcomes, and optimise production workflows to meet the diverse and evolving needs of the University community. This is an opportunity to join a highly service-focused team where your technical expertise, attention to detail and commitment to customer service will make a direct contribution to the success of teaching, research and operational activities across UniSC. You will work closely with colleagues and customers across the University to deliver efficient, innovative and responsive print solutions. You will Provide expert print services in digital, wide format, signage and finishing services across all UniSC locations; Coordination preparation, imposition and quotation of files for output for internal or external production while meeting required specifications; and Assist in the management and service of multifunctional devices (MFDs) and provide technical advice for the self-serve printing system (MyPrint). About you You are a technically skilled print production professional who takes pride in delivering high-quality outcomes and exceptional customer service. With extensive experience operating digital print and finishing equipment, you combine strong attention to detail with a practical, solutions-focused approach. You enjoy working collaboratively while also taking ownership of your workload in a fast-paced production environment. You will possess: Extensive experience in operating a wide range of high-volume digital printing, wide format and binding and finishing equipment; Exceptional attention to detail and ability to identify and correct defects; Provide strong analytical and problem solving skills; Proficiency in using digital tools for record keeping and machine operation; Skilled in various Imposition software programs including EFI Command Workstation, Flexi Print and Cut, Adobe Acrobat Pro; Commitment to high quality client service with clear communication skills; Understanding of Australian copyright legislation and requirements; Ability to work autonomously and as a cooperative team member and use initiative in a high-volume work environment to prioritise workloads, meet deadlines and support others as required; and Capacity to undertake the physical requirements of the position and awareness of Workplace Health and Safety legislation and requirements. Desirable Completion of the expert fiery cutsheet certificate. A current Queensland Class C driver’s licence. A current forklift licence. Don't meet every requirement? At UniSC, we understand that your work and life experiences can be just as valuable. If you're excited about this role but your CV doesn't align perfectly with our position description, we encourage you to apply anyway. You may be just the right candidate for this or one of our many other opportunities. UniSC is an equal opportunity employer, committed to diversity and inclusion. We encourage applications from all backgrounds, including those with disabilities, women in STEM, First Nations Peoples, and individuals of diverse cultures, genders, abilities, and experiences. We value achievement relative to opportunity and encourage your commentary on your achievements in this context. For additional support during the application process, please contact us at unisc-careers@usc.edu.au or call +61 7 5430 2830. How to apply All applications must be lodged through our website. To apply please visit our website at: Careers at UniSC Applications for this position close midnight, Wednesday 30 September 2026. Position description: 493769_Print Production Officer.pdf Your completed application must include: a resume and a statement of suitability (not to exceed two pages) , which will be reviewed in alignment to the specified selection criteria as outlined within the position description. Further information regarding how to prepare your application is available on our website: Join our team. Have questions or want to know more? For a confidential discussion, please contact: Kim Luck Manager, Print Servies – Print Services Telephone: 07 5430 1121 Email: kluck@usc.edu.au We would love the opportunity to get to know you better, but we know it works both ways. To get to know a little more about us, visit us at: Welcome to UniSC and LinkedIn Life UniSC values a diverse and talented workforce and invites applications from candidates who already have legal work rights in Australia. UniSC does not accept unsolicited applications. For agency inquiries, contact unisc-careers@usc.edu.au Our Culture & Benefits: Our collaborative, passionate and welcoming culture is what really sets us apart. Modern teaching & research facilities. Professional development and career pathway opportunities. We are a proud recipient of the prestigious Athena SWAN Bronze Award, granted as part of the Science in Australia Gender Equity (SAGE) initiative. Flexible work arrangements & generous leave options. Salary packing options + 17% Super. EAP, fitness passport & discounted private health. Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:47 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:47 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles subtitles settings , opens subtitles settings dialog subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNTIES Apply now! Enter your details below to commence your application: First Name (required) 6e037823 Last Name (required) 3ac824bc Email (required) 51003b20 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you About UniSC For more information about UniSC's employment benefits and culture, including employee blogs, visit our employer information page . Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 3:17 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 3:17 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles subtitles settings , opens subtitles settings dialog subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. Recommended for you Project Coordinator UniSC Sunshine Coast Individual contributor, L6 $95,986 - $103,873 +17% super, School of Business and Creative Industries Join UniSC and help deliver a four-year Queensland Government-funded project that supports Queensland businesses to build capability and long-term sustainability through practical learning. Project Support Officer UniSC Sunshine Coast Administration / Admin Support, Individual contributor, L5 $82,843 - $93,358 +17% super, School of Business and Creative Industries Join UniSC and support the delivery of a Queensland Government-funded initiative that helps Queensland businesses build capability through practical learning. Functional Analyst - CRM UniSC Sunshine Coast Individual contributor, L7 $105,843 - $115,703 +17% super, Professional, Student Services, Technical Support Behind every great student experience is a network of systems, processes and people working together seamlessly. As our next Functional Analyst - CRM, you'll play a key role in improving the technology and business processes that help students connect, engage and succeed throughout their journey at UniSC. Technician  (Allied Health - Paramedicine) UniSC Sunshine Coast Academic Support Unit, Individual contributor, L5 $82,843 - $93,358 +17% super, Technical Support Provide technical support and expertise for Paramedicine practical and simulation classes, ensuring smooth delivery, quality learning, and successful student outcomes. Join our talent community! Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 57074298 Last Name (required) 00c15905 Email (required) f044aaf6 Job Alert bfeaa6aa Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Individual contributor L4 $76,275 - $80,218 +17% super Print Services Professional Individual contributor L4 $76,275 - $80,218 +17% super Print Services Professional Employment Type Full-Time Full-Time Locations UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia Send Please wait... Done Not You? Congratulations from the UniSC Talent Acquisition Team, you are now signed up for UniSC job alerts. Apply now! Enter your details below to commence your application: First Name (required) 52a99c0f Last Name (required) 60515940 Email (required) 32137a21 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 3:17 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 3:17 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles subtitles settings , opens subtitles settings dialog subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. T